  "body": "**Stacked on #4221** (the 2D slice of #1122, which is stacked on #4220 and #4218). The 2D slice names five fields that this guard finds. Until the chain merges, this diff also shows the commits of the three parents (42ca7bfc5, 9886fef31, b852d7257). The commit of this PR is cf3565107. After each parent merges, I merge `main` into this branch.\n\n## What changed\n\nSlice 3 of #1119: the operation pages. Each input on each operation page tab now has an accessible name.\n\n- **The cause.** On `main` 773736856, 1,840 of 1,861 input occurrences on the operation pages had no name. `num` and `combo` set no `labelled_by`. Only the `*_row` variants did, and the pages call the base helpers.\n- **A property row names its controls.** `prop_row` opens its row while it draws the row's controls (`layout::named_by`). The seam's fields drawn inside the row take its label as their name (`layout::name_by_row`). These fields are:\n  - `num` and its variants, and `num_plain`;\n  - `value_with_unit`;\n  - `combo`, `combo_owned` and `tool_combo`;\n  - `drag_row` (from #4221).\n\n  A field outside an open row takes no name from the seam. Thus a field never takes the name of the row drawn before it, which `row_label_id` (the last row of the frame) could give.\n- **The operation header** is a `Grid` with its own labels. Its Tool, Source, Setup and Coolant combos are named through `named_by` with their row labels.\n- **Spindle speed** (`spindle_row.rs`) is named by its row.\n- **No label twice.** `num_row`, `num_feed_row`, `num_plain_row` and `num_unit_row` already named by the row. They are now the same field as their bases, so no field has the same label two times.\n- **Files.** The helpers are in the new file `layout/row_name.rs` (49 lines). `layout/form.rs` grows by 4 lines (420 to 424). It was over the 400-line limit before this PR.\n- **Tests that read a row's text.** Seven tests found a row's text with `get_by_label`. The row's control now has the same name, so they now ask for the `Label` node (`get_by_role_and_label(Role::Label, ..)`). In `wire_page_tests`, a click on the row label opened the named combo, so a small `show_row` helper scrolls the label into view instead. No assertion changes.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1119-op-page-names.md`.\n\nNothing visible changes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::op_page_names::every_operation_page_tab_names_every_input` (new). It walks every kind of the registry and every tab that the kind has, as `every_registry_kind_gets_its_tab_bar` does. It fails on an input with no name, or with one label named twice. Each failure line names the kind, the tab, the role and the row text. The walk reached more than 500 inputs.\n  - On the 2D branch (before this commit), it is red with 667 lines. These are the header combos on each kind (Tool 205, Source 205, Coolant 202), Spindle speed (48), and the rest. On `main`, 5 more fields are red, which #4221 and #4218 fix.\n- Changed tests, now green:\n  - `dialog_tests::contour_side_is_a_same_row_field`\n  - `heights_tests::notes::chamfer_geometry_exposes_tip_offset`\n  - `sinker_pass_tests::a_rough_op_shows_its_pass_and_the_finished_cavity_size`\n  - `tests::rotary_flow_page::the_flow_passes_tab_draws_the_axis_group_the_band_rows_and_the_guide_hint`\n  - `tests::rotary_stated_axis::the_help_text_follows_the_resolver_machine_line_first`\n  - `wire_page::tests::wire_four_axis_states_the_stand_off_choice_and_the_verify_tolerance`\n  - `wire_page::tests::wire_sync_pick_button_arms_and_says_the_next_click`\n- The earlier #1119 guards stay green: `the_machine_page_names_every_input`, `the_machines_pane_names_every_input`, the fixture dialog and row guards, and the machine editor guards.\n\nNo new test binary (#3187). The new file is a module of the `camcraft-ui` lib tests (`egui_app/tests.rs`).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe 2D Contour Heights tab, from the off-screen renderer (`egui_kittest` with the headless wgpu device) at 620 x 1400, cropped to the top 560 px. The names are AccessKit data only. A pixel comparison of the full frames gives 0 different pixels. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork.\n\n| Before (b852d7257) | After (cf3565107) |\n|---|---|\n| ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1119-op-pages/before-contour-heights.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1119-op-pages/after-contour-heights.png) |\n\n## Gates\n\nOn cf3565107:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.6 min). It includes `ui suites: lib`.\n- The other `crates/ui` suites, run one by one: `egui_app` 8, `operations` 31, `shell` 21, `fixtures` 7, `machine` 7, `models` 4, `edge_loop_pick` 4 and `feedback` 7. All passed.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none. The pixel snapshots (release lane) were not run. The change draws no pixel.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No screen reader run. The names are checked in the AccessKit tree.\n- Inputs that a check box or a choice hides are not reached by the walk. They draw through the same seam.\n- Pages other than the operation pages (setup, WCS, stock, tool editor, dialogs) are not walked. They are the next #1119 slices, and many use `prop_row`, so they gain names from this change too.\n\nChangelog: Every input on the operation pages has an accessible name for screen readers (the row label it stands on).\n\nRefs #1119\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
